        "text": "Never use standard PLC inputs or non-safety boolean gates for primary operator point-of-operation safeguarding. A single welded contact, short circuit, or taped button must never be capable of initiating a machine stroke. Functional safety requires hardware-level anti-tie-down, 500 ms synchronism, anti-repeat, and cross-monitored dual safety valves."
