        "type": "markdown",
        "content": "## 3. Stage 1: The Naive Bypass Flaw (Why Boolean AND Fails)\n\nTo understand why traditional ladder logic fails, examine the Stage 1 circuit below. It implements simple concurrence: `stroke = pb1 AND pb2`.\n\nBecause the circuit only evaluates static boolean states without detecting dynamic signal transitions, it has zero anti-tie-down protection. If one button is bridged or wedged, the press is permanently converted into a single-button foot-switch equivalent."
