        "type": "markdown",
        "content": "## 6. Commissioning Checklist & Mandatory Plant Floor Proof Testing\n\nBefore putting any hydraulic press, mechanical stamper, or pneumatic cutter into active production with two-hand controls, safety engineers must perform and document these five mandatory tests:\n\n- **1. Anti-Tie-Down Proof Test:** Press and hold PB-101A for 5 seconds. While still holding PB-101A, press PB-101B. The press ram must not move. Repeat the test holding PB-101B and pressing PB-101A.\n- **2. Synchronism Window Verification:** Use a dual-channel calibrated timer to press PB-101A and PB-101B with a 600 ms stagger. Confirm that the safety controller rejects the actuation and indicates a synchronism timing fault.\n- **3. Interrupted Stroke & Re-initiation Test:** Initiate a valid downstroke. During the downward motion, release PB-101A while keeping PB-101B pressed. The ram must stop immediately within its certified stopping time. While still holding PB-101B, re-press PB-101A: the ram must remain halted until both buttons have been completely released.\n- **4. Dynamic Spool Position Discrepancy Test:** Disconnect or override the spool position feedback switch on Valve A. Attempt to initiate a stroke: the safety controller must detect the cross-monitoring discrepancy, trip the fault output, and lock out the hydraulic pump.\n- **5. Certified Safety Distance Measurement:** Measure the stopping time of the ram using an optical stop-time measurement device across 10 maximum-speed downstrokes. Recalculate $S = (1600 \\times T_{\\text{max}}) + C$ and verify that the physical console distance equals or exceeds the calculated distance."
